    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** anchoring the offensive core, boasting an elite score of 73.66. His matchup against Bieber is highly favorable given the 5.25 xERA and the boost from dynamic platoon advantages, setting him up for a high-ceiling performance. **Drake Baldwin** is another cornerstone of today\u2019s strategy; batting lead-off against Pfaadt gives him an excellent runway to capitalize on his 67.49 efficiency score. We are also monitoring the conditions for **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**, who benefit from a 64.71 and 66.24 score respectively; the \"wind out\" factor at their venue provides a meaningful boost to their power projections against the southpaw Gasser, offsetting the slightly lower lineup positioning for **Kyle Tucker**.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jackson Merrill**, who fell just short of the starting threshold with a score of 50.99. While his recency bias is strong, the matchup against Williams (2.90 xERA) presented too much risk to displace our current starters, particularly with the premium we place on the lineup stability of players like **Coby Mayo** and **Gunnar Henderson**. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a lower score (55.72) due to a challenging platoon matchup, his dual-threat potential\u2014specifically his ability to exploit a slow pitcher delivery for stolen bases\u2014keeps him in the lineup. Note that we are still tracking \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Jacob Wilson**, **Wade Meckler**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**; any significant shift in their batting order could necessitate a late-cycle adjustment to maintain our efficiency targets. **Jordan Westburg** remains unavailable on the IL, and while players like **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** provide depth, they remain below the floor required to displace our high-efficiency starters today.",
